@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@* EPIC 30 Sprint 30.23 (BD30-F065): before this component existed, an unhandled exception thrown
   from any page's render tree or event handler tore down the entire SignalR circuit — the user saw
   the exact same generic "connection lost, trying to reconnect" experience as a real network blip,
   with no distinguishable "something in the app broke" message and no recovery beyond a full page
   reload the user had to think to try themselves. Wrapping @Body in this component (via
   LoggingErrorBoundary, the stock ErrorBoundary with server-side logging added) keeps the circuit
   alive and renders this branded fallback instead.

   Lab adaptation (Sprint 33.8, FE33-016): the BeeDay source injects IStringLocalizer<DesignSystemResources>
   for the three fallback strings below. The Lab has no localization pipeline (Program.cs has no
   AddLocalization, confirmed against the already-copied BeeDayIcon which also has no localizer
   dependency), so introducing one now would be scope creep — these are plain hardcoded English
   strings instead, taken verbatim from DesignSystemResources.en-US.resx at extraction time. *@
<LoggingErrorBoundary>
    <ChildContent>
        @ChildContent
    </ChildContent>
    <ErrorContent>
        <div class="beeday-error-boundary" role="alert">
            <BeeDayEmptyState Title="Something went wrong"
                              Description="This page ran into an unexpected problem. Reloading usually fixes it."
                              Icon="BeeDayIconName.ValidationError" />
            <BeeDayButton Variant="BeeDayButtonVariant.Primary" OnClick="Reload">Reload page</BeeDayButton>
        </div>
    </ErrorContent>
</LoggingErrorBoundary>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    // A full reload establishes a brand new circuit rather than calling ErrorBoundary.Recover() to
    // resume the same one — the component tree state that led to the exception is not known to be
    // safe to resume, so starting clean is the predictable, safe default recovery action.
    private void Reload() => Navigation.NavigateTo(Navigation.Uri, forceLoad: true);
}
